Z||000000||Black88GT||11-20-2000||07:57 PM||||Just curious to see if anyone here collects any type of WW2 memorobilia.  My friends dad has this awesome collection of Nazi and fascist Italy stuff, it prompted me to want to start collecting.  I see on Ebay they have a bunch of stuff and even found a few websites.  Anyone out there into it?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||11-20-2000||09:18 PM||||umm... interesting hobby... and here I was, thinking that rock collecting was pretty hardcore.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||11-20-2000||09:55 PM||||Back in High School I had a friend who's Dad was stationed in Germany for four years. Of course he was there as well and started collecting WWII stuff. He had some interesting stuff... a Panzer helment, a couple of daggers, and dress sword, a bunh of medals, and a couple of unforms -- one being Gestopo (sp?).<P>He said he found most of the going "barn rading" (read: stealing). He said he never go into trouble with the local officials because it's illegal for German residence to have the stuff. I guess it's that whole Nazi/Hitler thing. Anyway, I always found the stuff interesting.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-21-2000||11:29 AM||||Have a few nazi medals and stuff. Don't remember what all is there. Most of it is at my sister's house.<BR>Have an old .32 semi-auto. Made in a German-occupied French factory. Has a nazi eagle engraved in the side. Not in real great condition. Not worth much to a collector. <BR>Not real good as a "carry" gun. Would be afraid to run modern ammo through it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||11-21-2000||03:00 PM||||Raydar, interested in selling or trading for fiero parts?  Just a thought...<P>You can't own ANYTHING Nazi in France or Germany.  I noticed on all of the ebay auctions it had that they could not ship to those countries.  Gee I wonder why?<P>I<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
